# fixedbugs, defect 2051, 2026-10-13, a record's variable.
#
# SYMPTOM: a header of the program's own holding `struct counted { int n; }
# malloc;` was told `internal error: compiling the generated C failed` at
# exit 2, as the reproducer was: clang's notes at the generated unit's
# include line.
#
# FIX: told as C's own `malloc`, which clang declares itself at the
# header's line, the header refused at its line 3, exit 1, with a `guess`
# fix renaming it (`cli/builtin_name.hero`).

extern "fixedbugs-2051-a-header-that-declares-a-c-library-function-as-a-record-is-refused.h"  #~ ffi_header_refused
    function eight() -> i32

function main()
    print(eight())
